<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_SumpDuskLock.xml                   UtinniPatches · SUMP_MECHANICS_1 (S6)
  ============================================================================
  sump_kit_spec.md S6 "the lock": "reuse ruled RM_GameCondition_
  EnvironmentalWeather as a permanent biomeMapConditions entry  — forced
  RUT_SumpWeather... never vanilla's rain-capable rotation." Attached to
  RUT_Sump via Patches/RUT_SumpDuskLock_BiomeWiring.xml (same pass), not a
  direct edit to RUT_Sump.xml's own biomeMapConditions  — this Def only
  exists when mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards is active (whole-Def
  MayRequire, matching RUT_ScaldSteamLock.xml / RUT_MiasmaWeatherLock.xml's
  own precedent, this same folder), so a bare <li> baked directly into the
  always-loaded BiomeDef would be a dangling cross-reference the moment that
  mod is absent. BiomeConditionMapComponent.MapGenerated() ->
  GameConditionMaker.MakeConditionPermanent(...) is what actually makes a
  biomeMapConditions entry run forever (Verse/RimWorld/
  BiomeConditionMapComponent.cs:12-22, confirmed against the live 1.6
  decompile this pass)  — no extra field on this Def does that job.

  No damageDef/hediffToApply/carrierHediff and no density factors: unlike
  Miasma's own lock (which bootstraps a hediff carrier and a plant-growth
  bonus), the sheet gives the Sump's dusk itself no damage or growth effect
   — only the weather override. The Sump's own animalDensity/plantDensity
  figures already live on the BiomeDef (RUT_Sump.xml, BIOME_OWNERSHIP_WAVE_1),
  and "the light" (darkness, not the weather) is the SEPARATE
  BiomeGlowMultiplierExtension wired directly onto RUT_Sump.xml's own
  modExtensions in this same pass  — this Def does not touch glow at all.

  allowUnderground false: a surface weather-lock has no business reaching the
  bumbledrone hives beneath the tar (the_sump.md §0's "subterranean...
  colonies tunneling beneath the insulating tar")  — matches
  RUT_MiasmaWeatherLock.xml's own choice for the same reasoning, not
  RUT_ScaldSteamLock.xml's (that biome's steam genuinely reaches its own
  underground spaces).

  MayRequire is load-bearing: conditionClass and the modExtension both live
  in mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards.

  ❓ owed, out of this pass's no-bridge scope (per the kit spec's own build
  order and this task's instructions): the live glow-multiplier calibration
  check. This Def's own contribution  — the weather lock itself  — needs no
  live check; GameCondition.ForcedWeather() is read and confirmed
  unconditional (GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather.cs:198-202).
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GameConditionDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_SumpDuskLock</defName>
    <conditionClass>RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather</conditionClass>
    <label>permanent dusk</label>
    <description>The Sump never sees full day or full dark. The sun sits just below the horizon, forever, and it does not rain.</description>
    <canBePermanent>true</canBePermanent>
    <allowUnderground>false</allowUnderground>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.EnvironmentalWeatherExtension">
        <forcedWeather>RUT_SumpWeather</forcedWeather>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </GameConditionDef>

</Defs>
